 vacation was that the pokemon died  what's even stranger is that after  defeating a trainer and seeing red  received $200 for winning the battle  commands would appear again if you  selected run the battle would end as it  normally does you could also select  curse if did upon returning to the  overworld the trainer sprite will be  gone after leaving and re-entering the  area a spot where the trainer had been  would be replaced with a tombstone like  the ones at lavender Tower  the move curse wasn't usable in all  instances it would fail against ghost  Pokemon it would also fail if it was  used against the trainers that you would  have to face again such as the arrival  or Giovanni it was usable in your final  battle against the myeloma I figured  this was a gimmick of the game allowing  you to use previously owned capturable  ghosts and because the curse made the  game so easy I essentially used it  throughout the whole adventure the game  changed quite a bit after defeating the  Elite Four after viewing the Hall of  Fame which consists of ghosts and a  couple of Pokemon I use for HMS the  screen cut the black  a box appeared with the words many years  later that then cut the lavender town an  old man was standing looking at  tombstones he then realized this man was  your character the man moved at only  half of your normal walking speed you no  longer had any Pokemon with you not even  ghost who up to this point have been  impossible to remove from your party  through depositing in the PC the  overworld  was entirely empty there was no people  at all there were still tombstones of  the trainers that used curse on  you could go pretty much anywhere in the  overworld at this point though your  movement was limited by the fact he had  no Pokemon to use a gems and regardless  of where you went the music of lavender  town continued on an infinite loop after  wandering for a while I found that if  you go through diglettz cave one of the  cuttable bushes that normally blocks the  path and the other side is no longer  there allowing me to advance and return  to Pallet Town  upon entering your house and going to  the exact tile where you start the game  the screen would cut the black  then a sprite of Caterpie appeared it  was replaced by wheedle and then Pidgey  I soon realized as the Pokemon  progressed from Rattata to Blastoise  that these were all of the Pokemon that  I had used curse on after the end of my  rivals team a youngster appeared and  then a bug catcher  these were the trainers I had cursed  throughout the sequence the lavender  town music was playing but it was slowly  decreasing in pitch by the time your  rival appeared on screen it was a little  more than a demonic rumble another cut  to black a few moments later the battle  screen suddenly appeared  your trainer sprite was now that of an  old man the same one as the one who  teaches you how to catch a Pokemon in  Viridian City ghost appears on the other  side along with the words ghost wants to  fight  he couldn't use items and you had no  Pokemon if he tried to run you couldn't  escape the only option was a fight using  fight would immediately cause you to  struggle which didn't affect ghosts but  it did chip off a bit of your own HP  when it was ghosts turned to attack that  would simply say dot dot dot eventually  when your HP reached a critical point  ghost would finally used curse the  screen cut to black for a final time  regardless of the buttons pressed you  were permanently stuck in this black  screen  at this point the only thing you could  do was turn the Gameboy off when you  played again new game was the only  option the game and erased the file I  played through this hacked game many  many times and every time the game ended  with this sequence several times I  didn't use ghost at all though he was  impossible to remove from the party in  these cases it didn't show any Pokemon  or trainers and simply cut to the  climactic battle with ghost I'm not su